WEBVTT

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:12.290
"Song of the Fallen Angel"

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.420
The Fallen Angel is in chains.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.920
Wings ripped off,
consumed by prejudice...

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.300
About to draw her last breath
in a pitch-black world of despair...

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.590
Do you know her name?

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:29.100
In time, will she be driven
to the realm of oblivion,

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.560
and return to a world of nothingness?

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:32.730
No!

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:34.650
Her requiem will turn into a roar,

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.400
and she'll tear off the mask of hypocrisy!

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.570
Vanquishing cowards, ripping
myths apart at the seams...

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:42.360
Do you know her name?

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.990
That's right, her name is...

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.030
What could it be?

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:52.040
Wh-Wh-Wh-What the heck? Why?

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.040
Why is this on the ground?

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.790
I know that I put it away in my bag!

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.290
Anyway, why did you read it?

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.750
Who do you think you are?

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.050
Drive yourself to the realm
of oblivion right now!

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.230
Thank goodness about Nanako-chan.

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:20.780
Now I'm pissed all over again
at that bastard, Namatame!

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.280
For what he put
Nanako-chan through!

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:28.030
Yeah, but Namatame only owned up
to the incidents after Amagi's.

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:32.370
Meaning that someone else was behind
what happened to Konishi and Yamano, right?

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:35.790
If we're to believe
what he told us, yes.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:40.420
There was no stamp on that envelope,
and it wasn't addressed to anyone.

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:44.590
From this, we can surmise that the culprit
dropped it himself into Senpai's mailbox...

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:45.760
Senpai?

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.140
What's wrong?

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:48.550
Sorry.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:49.930
What is it?

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:52.100
Senpai, what's the matter?

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:54.100
For some reason,

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.600
he seems to be hesitating.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.560
He's wavering...

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:02.780
It's like he's going to
vanish, and that scares me.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:10.240
That might be the effect of
one of the Arcana he's obtained.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.500
The Fool.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:21.920
But at this time, this
Arcana is extremely unstable.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:26.590
This might very well be a sign of change.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:33.890
Inaba Municipal Hospital

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:40.440
For God's sake, can't
you even shop right?

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.320
You should know that an occasion
like this calls for apples.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.400
Your mind-set is just too old-school.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.320
What did you say?

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:49.990
Hey, simmer down. If you get mad,
your stitches will burst open.

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:52.740
Then don't do anything
to make me mad!

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:54.290
Whoa, you're so scary!

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:57.330
I'm going to go see how
Nanako-chan's doing, okay?

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:58.000
Hey, don't run off!

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:01.080
<i>Is that you, Yu? What's up?</i>

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:05.050
Uncle, is Adachi-san
at the station today?

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.550
<i>No, he was just here with me.</i>

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:10.430
<i>Right now, he should be
checking on Nanako.</i>

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:50.470
Hey.

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:53.350
I thought you'd be showing up.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:59.100
What's wrong? You came because
you wanted to see me, right?

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:00.600
Well, talk to me.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:03.560
Adachi-san...

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:06.270
Go on, ask me.

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:11.200
"Were you the one who shoved Ms. Yamano
and Saki Konishi into the TV world?"

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:16.450
Talk about anti-climactic, though.
Coming here on your own.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.240
What happened to your friends?

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:21.120
Let me see you playing
wannabe detectives till the end.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.710
I really get a kick
out of that, you know.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.130
The whole gang should come together.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:29.590
Joining forces to take out the bad guys.

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:31.630
Friendship, effort, victory?

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:34.340
You guys love that stuff, don't you?

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.430
I wanted to talk to you.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:38.350
At least one more time.

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:39.810
Just the two of us?

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:42.770
Well, I don't have
anything to say to you.

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:44.850
Why did it come to this?

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.570
I just told you I had nothing to say.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:48.860
Hear me out!

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:50.650
Something wrong with your hearing?

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:52.240
But I believed in you!

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:57.990
What's up with that?

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:03.250
What you believed in was a version of me that
you made up in your own mind, am I right?

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:06.130
You believed in me on your own,
and you were betrayed on your own,

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:09.250
so where do you get off
complaining to me?

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:12.880
It's all over.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.510
Please turn yourself in, Adachi-san.

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:19.470
You have a way of saying
stupid things, don't you?

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:22.270
I'm sure that Dojima-san would
want the same thing!

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:29.400
People like you who come up to me,
thinking you'll talk sense into me...

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.400
You piss me off the most.

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:35.450
Come on...

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:37.280
Magatsu Izanagi!

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:38.780
Izanagi!

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:46.790
What a surprise.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:50.000
They're dead ringers, our Personas.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.130
Talk about ironic...

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:56.380
Adachi-san, if you insist on doing this,

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:58.890
then I'm going to stop you!

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.260
I told you...

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:03.770
That kind of thing is so...

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:57.030
Tennis Club
Members Needed!!

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:13.800
Award

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.560
Official Notification

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:26.180
<i>At the end of the day,
it's all about talent.</i>

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:28.890
<i>Those who have it will succeed
no matter what they do.</i>

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:32.060
<i>Those who don't will
fail no matter what.</i>

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:01.180
<i>My nephew will be coming
to stay with me tomorrow...</i>

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:41.880
This whole world is crap!

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:46.890
For some reason...

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:48.640
Can we leave it at that?

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:50.680
Stop it.

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:54.650
I'm sure that both Dojima-san
and Nanako would be thrilled.

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:56.520
Don't look at me.

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:59.570
Because I'm just
doing this on my own.

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:01.570
What do you know?

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:05.490
There's no profit or loss involved
when you're helping each other out.

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:07.030
Get out of my sight!

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:12.120
What was that?

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:15.130
What a masterpiece!

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:18.210
I saw it. I felt it.

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:20.800
The world from your perspective.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:23.970
Meaning that you saw it too, right?

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:26.300
The world from my perspective?

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:28.810
Go on home now.

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:31.560
To your little friends.

00:09:31.890 --> 00:09:33.020
I...

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:40.820
You really creep me out,
you know that?

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:54.500
This is the other ordeal that
our client must go through.

00:10:03.010 --> 00:10:04.380
Welcome back.

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:06.470
Yosuke...

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:09.890
I thought you were acting strange.

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:11.720
So I was right, huh?

00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:13.850
Sorry.

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:15.230
That's okay.

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:18.020
You did have some
kind of plan, didn't you?

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:18.980
But, hey...

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:21.610
You should believe in us more.

00:10:23.650 --> 00:10:26.030
And try not to make us worry.

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:28.370
Or make Marie-chan worry, either.

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:35.210
Hey...

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:37.960
There's something
on your mind, right?

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:42.250
I can't tell what it is
if you don't say anything.

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:47.380
Was it self-satisfaction, I wonder?

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:50.970
Saying it was for
someone else's sake...

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:54.640
was I just being
condescending and selfish?

00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:00.520
Because of that, I ended up
driving someone to the edge,

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:02.770
and both Nanako and Adachi-san...

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:05.360
Maybe it just didn't mean anything...

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:07.280
all that I've done...

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:10.240
You're so annoying.

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:12.410
You're annoying.

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:14.870
Spineless. I don't want to hear it!

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:16.750
Marie...

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.290
Come with me.

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:25.010
What's going on?

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:26.550
I can't see a thing.

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:28.260
It's not what I thought it was.

00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:33.510
Hey, do you remember?

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:37.060
That day that you first came here?

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:41.690
You said you'd help me search
for my memories, remember?

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:43.270
But it was a total bust.

00:11:43.270 --> 00:11:45.070
I haven't remembered anything.

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:46.570
Total failure.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:48.320
Sorry...

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:53.240
But on the other hand, you gave me
lots of memories, didn't you?

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:56.870
Shopping. You kept
running off somewhere.

00:11:57.120 --> 00:11:59.460
The beach... That
old guy was creepy.

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:01.540
Fireworks... They were so dazzling.

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:03.790
The quiz show... That was stupid.

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:05.880
The band... I wore out my fingers.

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:07.340
But it made me happy.

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:08.670
I was excited.

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:10.430
My heart was pounding.

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:14.470
They're all my precious memories.

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:19.430
It was you who gave them
all to me, you know.

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:23.270
So why are you saying that
they didn't mean anything?

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:26.780
Marie...

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:30.650
I don't care if it's selfish or
condescending or anything!

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:32.610
Even if it was...

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:34.410
it made me happy!

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:38.040
Don't say that it was meaningless!

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:39.910
The memories you created for me...

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.420
...don't say that they never existed!

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:51.800
I see.

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:53.800
You're right...

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:02.140
It's beautiful, isn't it?

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:03.520
I wonder why.

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:07.860
It feels like I've known
this view forever.

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:12.860
I want them all, after all.

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:18.620
My old memories and all
the memories I'm making with you.

00:13:19.370 --> 00:13:22.210
So I'm giving you
this to keep for me.

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:26.580
Whether I'm gonna search for
my memories, or make new ones,

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:28.960
it's gonna be with you
no matter what.

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:31.590
So it would be the same
even if you had it, right?

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:33.380
But you have to promise...

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:35.220
That you'll give it back.

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:37.350
If you disappear with it on you...

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:38.890
I'll never forgive you.

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:40.390
All right.

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:41.770
I promise.

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:45.100
I'm not going to waver anymore.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:49.020
Even if there are people I've
hurt because of what I've done...

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:53.780
Even still, the bond we have
together... It's genuine...

00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:54.860
Yes.

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:56.450
Hey!

00:13:59.490 --> 00:14:00.540
Yosuke...

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:01.580
You guys.

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:03.790
We're not letting you
go off on your own again!

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:06.120
I'll always be by your side, Sensei!

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:12.840
People only see what they want to see,
and believe only what they want to believe.

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:15.380
But you're not like that, are you?

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:18.390
You guys... Let's go!

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:32.780
I can sense Shadows
lurking all over the place!

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:33.780
Bring it on!

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:36.070
I'll pulverize every last one of them!

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:38.950
Yu, you head over to
where Adachi-san is!

00:14:39.490 --> 00:14:42.580
Didn't I tell you to believe in us?

00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:46.830
Gotcha.

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:51.670
Hey, how cool is that?

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:54.670
The hero arriving on the scene?

00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:00.760
Well, don't you look like
you've taken a load off.

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:03.520
Adachi-san, I reject you!

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:04.770
Oh, yeah?

00:15:05.270 --> 00:15:06.140
Persona!

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:13.570
Mada!

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:19.860
Futsunushi!

00:15:25.160 --> 00:15:28.250
There you go again, relying on it...

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:31.000
The power of that
thing you call a bond!

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:33.420
Scathach!

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:42.300
Effort, love, hope...

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:44.310
Not to mention bonds...

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:47.520
Hey, it's like a morality textbook!

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:48.980
What's wrong with that?

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:52.610
It's shallow, that's what!

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:56.070
Okay, then tell me - what's a bond?

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:58.280
To believe.

00:15:58.280 --> 00:16:01.240
In the person at your
side - in your friends!

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:20.260
You don't get it, do you?

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:22.590
That's why you're such a loser.

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:28.930
The word "believe" is
a curse that crushes people.

00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:32.900
There's no way that you can read
someone else's mind, is there?

00:16:33.270 --> 00:16:39.360
What you believe in is your own selfish ideal of
how you want a certain person to be - nothing more.

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:40.860
That's not true!

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:47.450
And in fact, you forced that on me.

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:50.460
And now you're thinking
that I betrayed you, right?

00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:52.670
What are you, a moron?

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:02.010
Shut up!

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:07.720
But lucky you.

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:11.310
I don't think your friends
will ever turn on you.

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:16.190
You've seen each other's ugly
sides, how pathetic you can be,

00:17:16.190 --> 00:17:20.610
but you're like, "Oh, that's okay" -
pretending to be generous, smiling.

00:17:20.610 --> 00:17:22.360
That's so creepy.

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:25.700
As if you could actually
like someone's ugly side!

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:26.780
Moron!

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:36.920
Trying so hard not to hurt others because
you don't want to get hurt yourself!

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:39.460
Do you know what we call that?

00:17:39.880 --> 00:17:41.840
Licking each other's wounds!

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:45.800
That's what this "bond"
thing of yours is all about!

00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:48.720
No, it's not!

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:50.520
That can't possibly be true!

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:55.060
We've always accepted
who we really are!

00:17:55.060 --> 00:17:59.940
Even if we got hurt, we've come
all this way in search of the truth!

00:18:03.570 --> 00:18:07.660
See, that's just more whitewashing!

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:11.790
You guys...

00:18:12.160 --> 00:18:14.210
...really piss me off!

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:27.800
So what if it is whitewashing?

00:19:20.230 --> 00:19:23.070
Dammit, this is lame.

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:25.070
So it's all over now?

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:27.740
You and me...

00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:34.200
Ending up so differently, when
we have the same power...

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:36.500
Why do you think that is?

00:19:38.710 --> 00:19:41.000
I know...

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:43.170
Because you have a bond...

00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:45.420
that's what you're gonna say, right?

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:47.260
You make me sick.

00:19:58.810 --> 00:20:00.940
You had one yourself...

00:20:02.150 --> 00:20:04.400
Let's go back, Adachi-san...

00:20:11.530 --> 00:20:12.410
Adachi-san!

00:20:13.280 --> 00:20:14.910
Adachi-san!

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:28.760
Adachi-san.

00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:37.060
I can't even watch anymore.

00:20:49.900 --> 00:20:51.400
I'm taking you back!

00:21:15.510 --> 00:21:16.720
What?

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:18.770
It is time to awaken.

00:21:18.770 --> 00:21:19.970
Who are you?

00:21:20.390 --> 00:21:22.560
Ameno-sagiri has been slain.

00:21:22.850 --> 00:21:26.110
The fog shall return
to its rightful place...

00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:28.860
What?

00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:33.410
I...

00:21:33.610 --> 00:21:35.200
I...

00:21:36.070 --> 00:21:37.740
I see.

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:39.830
I...

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:46.500
It's over, huh?

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:47.670
Yeah.

00:21:49.130 --> 00:21:53.340
I can't stay with you all.

00:21:53.680 --> 00:21:58.680
But the memories you gave me
are my treasures. So...

00:21:59.560 --> 00:22:00.970
So...

00:22:01.470 --> 00:22:03.810
I'm taking them all with me, all right?

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:17.570
Is something wrong?

00:22:18.740 --> 00:22:20.950
No, it's nothing.

00:22:23.750 --> 00:22:25.500
Goodbye...

00:24:03.510 --> 00:24:05.810
The 24th... Are you free?

00:24:05.810 --> 00:24:07.810
What? The 24th?

00:24:07.810 --> 00:24:09.230
Yes! I'm free!

00:24:09.230 --> 00:24:11.100
Well, I am free, but...

00:24:11.100 --> 00:24:12.610
The 24th?

00:24:12.810 --> 00:24:14.190
I think I'm free.
